Set unix_socket_directories explicitly in the rendered Patroni configuration.
Upstream relies on the Debian/PGDG packages' compiled-in default of
/var/run/postgresql for both the server and libpq; the Docker Hardened
PostgreSQL packages keep the upstream source default (/tmp) on both sides. The
server therefore listens on /run/postgresql, which configure_spilo.py creates
and Patroni uses, and on /tmp, where the shipped libpq sends every client that
names no host (the psql calls in post_init.sh and on_role_change.sh, pgqd).
Upstream source: https://github.com/zalando/spilo/blob/4.1-p2/postgres-appliance/scripts/configure_spilo.py
diff --git a/postgres-appliance/scripts/configure_spilo.py b/postgres-appliance/scripts/configure_spilo.py
index 61f00ac..359fedc 100755
--- a/postgres-appliance/scripts/configure_spilo.py
+++ b/postgres-appliance/scripts/configure_spilo.py
@@ -289,6 +289,7 @@ postgresql:
   parameters:
     archive_command: {{{postgresql.parameters.archive_command}}}
     shared_buffers: {{postgresql.parameters.shared_buffers}}
+    unix_socket_directories: /run/postgresql, /tmp
     logging_collector: 'on'
     log_destination: csvlog
     log_directory: ../pg_log
